1
00:00:00,377 --> 00:00:05,482
The Library — Research from subject-matter experts, site visits and walkthroughs — written, organised and shared.

2
00:00:06,419 --> 00:00:11,274
The Library keeps the research behind the writing: SME interviews, site visits, walkthroughs and notes.

3
00:00:11,911 --> 00:00:15,313
Search it, and filter by kind, status or client.

4
00:00:15,933 --> 00:00:21,540
Each document shows its kind, its status, the client and project it's for — and any open questions.

5
00:00:24,265 --> 00:00:30,272
A document opens on the right, laid out and ready to read — with its headings, tables and the questions still waiting for an answer.

6
00:00:30,974 --> 00:00:33,484
Edit turns it into a word processor.

7
00:00:35,986 --> 00:00:41,992
The toolbar has what you'd expect — styles, bold and italic, lists, tables, links, images — and keyboard shortcuts.

8
00:00:42,681 --> 00:00:47,784
Insert adds content blocks: a note, a warning, a question for the SME, a step list…

9
00:00:52,686 --> 00:00:59,216
Writer tools help with the raw material — paste a dump of notes, and Organize turns it into headings, lists and a table of contents.

10
00:01:02,320 --> 00:01:07,423
Styles sets how headings and paragraphs look — for this document, or as the house style.

11
00:01:10,219 --> 00:01:16,248
The side panel also has the document's outline, its follow-ups — the open questions — its terms, links and details.

12
00:01:16,931 --> 00:01:20,734
Everything saves as you type. Done editing goes back to reading.

13
00:01:23,146 --> 00:01:28,750
New document starts a blank page or a template — an SME interview, a site visit, a walkthrough.

14
00:01:32,309 --> 00:01:36,424
Collect · organise · share — More help: the Handbook → The Library.
